CORE
main.c
--mmio-region 0x1000:256:weak _ --no-pointer-check --no-bounds-check
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
value read back from the region: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
--
A weakly-ordered MMIO region (--mmio-region addr:size:weak) returns a
non-deterministic value on read -- a sound over-approximation of reordering and
staleness -- so the read-back is not guaranteed to equal the written value. The
per-region device-memory type is recovered precisely from the region
declaration, without a points-to analysis.
